# DAAD Gathering schedule (this repo)

## What it is

Static **event schedule viewer** for **DAAD Gathering** (currently titled “2026” in `index.html`). Users browse lineup by day/stage, filter (date, stage, artist, tags, etc.), open sample-set links, and **download `.ics`** for selections or full schedule. No app backend in production: same behavior as **GitHub Pages** (HTML + client-side JS only).

## Stack & run locally

- **UI**: single-page `index.html` — Tailwind + theme tokens compiled to **`assets/app.css`** (run `npm run build:css` after changing markup / config), Font Awesome **`assets/fontawesome/`**, fonts **`assets/fonts/`** baked into **`assets/tailwind-input.css`** pipeline.
- **Companion page**: `downloads.html` (same visual language; **online-only** — no service worker; **not** part of PWA offline scope).
- **Dev server**: `server.py` — minimal `SimpleHTTPRequestHandler`, `/` → `index.html`, CORS `*` + no-store headers. Run: `python server.py` (default port **5500**).

## Data source (critical)

- **Canonical runtime data** is **`data/events.json`**: a **top-level JSON array** of event objects. **`fetchEvents()`** loads it with `fetch('./data/events.json')` — **no CSV** and **no live Sheet fetch** in the shipped app.
- **Authoring**: maintain **`data/events.csv`** as the checklist source in-repo. **`data/events.json`** is **generated only** via **`python3 scripts/csv_to_events.py`** (no args → reads **`data/events.csv`**, writes **`data/events.json`**). You may pass another CSV path; output defaults to **`data/events.json`** unless `--out`. Script uses **`Europe/Budapest`** (`zoneinfo`), same wall-clock semantics as **`EVENT_TIMEZONE`** in `index.html`.
- **CSV contract:** required headers **`id`** (integer), **`stage`**, **`band`**, **`date`**, **`time`** (12h), **`duration`**. **`duration`** column must exist on every row, but cells may be **blank** — the script substitutes **`1:00:00`** and prints a **`stderr`** line noting the row **`id`**.
- **Optional columns only:** sample-set URL column (matched with typo tolerance **`samlpe`**, same as legacy), **`tags`**. Fail fast if any required field is missing (`id`/stage/band/date/time cells), **`duration` is invalid when present**, **`id`** is not an integer / duplicates IDs, **`id`/time/date** parse failures.
- **`event.id`** in the app is the **integer `id` from CSV** (not derived from time + stage + title). Selections in **`localStorage`** use that id.
- **GViz** URL (`.../gviz/tq?tqx=out:csv`) and “do not use `/export?format=csv` in **browser** `fetch`” apply only to **legacy or tooling** if anything still requests the Sheet from JS. Prefer **`events.json`** as the single runtime path once migration is done.
- Constants in `index.html`: **`EVENT_TIMEZONE`** (`Europe/Budapest`). **End times in JSON** come from **start + `duration`** in **`csv_to_events.py`** (remove or stop using **`DEFAULT_SLOT_HOURS`** / next-slot inference in the app if no longer needed).
- **`data/events_2025.json`**: legacy snapshot only.
- **`ics/*.ics`**: bundled calendar files (older partial exports); in-app export uses **`generateIcsContent()`** in `index.html`.

## PWA / GitHub Pages

- Full checklist: **`.cursor/plans/pwa-implementation.md`** (manifest, `sw.js`, precache **`index.html`** shell + assets + `events.json`, iOS hint). **PWA ships only after** vendored **`assets/`** (Tailwind, Font Awesome, fonts).
- **`start_url` / `scope`** in **`manifest.json`** use **`./`** so the same artifact works locally and under **`aboros.github.io/daad/`**; service worker **`./sw.js`** registration matches.
- **`downloads.html`**: omit from service worker precache; do **not** register SW there.

## Implementation map (`index.html` script)

| Concern | Functions / notes |
|--------|-------------------|
| Fetch + events | **`fetchEvents`** → **`data/events.json`** (array). Objects include **`id`**, fields needed for schedule/ICS/cards (`summary`, `location`, `startUtcMs`, `endUtcMs`, `dayKey`, `duration`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `sampleSetUrl`, `tags`, …). |
| Times | Wall-clock semantics align with **`EVENT_TIMEZONE`**; producer is **`csv_to_events.py`**. |
| Stages | `normalizeStageName` → **uppercase** keys must align with **`STAGE_STYLES`** for colors |
| End times | **Defined in JSON** from CSV **`duration`** (plus start) in the script; app consumes **`endUtcMs` / `duration`** from loaded events. |
| UI | Filter/render helpers, tag filter, cards with `sampleSetUrl`, loading overlay + error banner |

When adding stages or columns, update **Sheet + `csv_to_events.py`**, **normalization**, and **`STAGE_STYLES`** together.
